-- Seed data for the Env Matrix Viewer.
--
-- Generated, and deliberately shaped:
--   * host and ip are unique per (env_instance, country, service, instance), so the baseline
--     contains no conflicts at all;
--   * four conflicts are then injected on purpose (see the `note` column) so the matrix has
--     something to highlight and the conflict panel is not empty on a fresh database:
--       1. CCS3 shares MS3's host:port          (UAT1/CN)  -> HOST_PORT
--       2. CCS2 shares MS2's ip:port            (UAT2/SG)  -> IP_PORT
--       3. MS4's http row reuses its https port (SIT1/MY)  -> HOST_PORT across schemes
--       4. CCS5 standby resolves to the active   (PROD1/HK) -> IP_PORT
--
-- Active-Standby (Green2) exists only in UAT and PROD; plain http only in SIT and UAT.

